WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
The tendon reaches the finger on a tangent and remains wrapped around its circular sector to the anchor.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The spool winds clockwise while the finger closes counterclockwise. The finger’s wrapped arc shortens as cord is taken up.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Sixty degrees at a 10 mm radius uses 10.47 mm of tendon. An 8 mm spool turns 75 degrees to take up that length.
